cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use StateSync-GKR in research, please cite this repository."
title: "StateSync-GKR"
abstract: >-
  StateSync-GKR is a Rust prover component that proves sparse-Merkle state
  transitions with a layered GKR protocol, compiling membership,
  non-membership, and single-leaf update operations into a layered arithmetic
  circuit and reducing that circuit through sumcheck. The operation semantics,
  a model of the verification-circuit compiler, the layer reduction, and their
  composition are mechanized in Isabelle/HOL across six registered sessions
  that build with no admitted proof, including soundness for the exact
  degree-four KoalaBear extension field the implementation uses. The Rust
  implementation is related to those models through a conditional forward
  verifier-acceptance theorem with an explicit Rust/model value-relation
  premise, recorded contract proofs for selected functions, differential
  tests, and adversarial vectors. The attached zkVM proof applies to the
  recorded historical v1.1 program.
type: software
